# LARAVEL COMMANDS CHEAT SHEET

This is a practical collection of commonly used Laravel commands for
day-to-day development.

---

1. STARTING / BASIC LARAVEL COMMANDS

---

1. Check Laravel version

php artisan --version

Explanation:
Shows the installed Laravel version.

---

2. Show all Artisan commands

php artisan list

Explanation:
Displays all available Laravel Artisan commands.

---

3. Get help for a command

php artisan help migrate

Explanation:
Shows available options and arguments for the "migrate" command.

You can replace "migrate" with any Artisan command.

Example:

php artisan help make:model

---

4. Start Laravel development server

php artisan serve

Explanation:
Starts Laravel's built-in development server.

Usually available at:

http://127.0.0.1:8000

---

5. Start server on another port

php artisan serve --port=8080

Explanation:
Starts the Laravel server on port 8080.

---

==================================================
2. ROUTES
=========

6. Display all routes

php artisan route:list

Explanation:
Shows all registered routes, HTTP methods, URIs, route names,
controllers, and middleware.

Very useful for debugging routes.

---

7. Display routes with more information

php artisan route:list -v

Explanation:
Shows additional route and middleware information.

---

8. Show API routes

php artisan route:list --path=api

Explanation:
Displays routes whose URL starts with /api.

---

9. Filter routes by name

php artisan route:list --name=users

Explanation:
Displays routes whose names contain "users".

---

10. Clear route cache

php artisan route:clear

Explanation:
Clears cached routes.

Useful when route changes are not being reflected.

---

11. Cache routes

php artisan route:cache

Explanation:
Caches routes for better production performance.

Do not use this casually during development if you frequently
change routes.

---

==================================================
3. CONTROLLERS
==============

12. Create a controller

php artisan make:controller UserController

Explanation:
Creates:

app/Http/Controllers/UserController.php

---

13. Create a resource controller

php artisan make:controller UserController --resource

Explanation:
Creates a controller containing methods commonly used for
CRUD operations:

index()
create()
store()
show()
edit()
update()
destroy()

---

14. Create an API controller

php artisan make:controller UserController --api

Explanation:
Creates a controller intended for API CRUD operations.

It does not include create() and edit(), since those are generally
used for HTML forms.

---

15. Create controller with model

php artisan make:controller UserController --model=User

Explanation:
Creates a controller associated with the User model.

---

==================================================
4. MODELS
=========

16. Create a model

php artisan make:model Product

Explanation:
Creates:

app/Models/Product.php

---

17. Create model + migration

php artisan make:model Product -m

Explanation:
Creates:

app/Models/Product.php
database/migrations/xxxx_xx_xx_create_products_table.php

---

18. Create model + factory + migration + seeder

php artisan make:model Product -mfs

Explanation:
Creates:

Model
Migration
Factory
Seeder

---

19. Create model with most related files

php artisan make:model Product -a

Explanation:
Creates the model and several related files such as:

Model
Factory
Migration
Seeder
Controller
Form Request

This is useful when starting a new CRUD resource.

---

==================================================
5. MIGRATIONS
=============

20. Create a migration

php artisan make:migration create_products_table

Explanation:
Creates a new migration file inside:

database/migrations/

---

21. Run migrations

php artisan migrate

Explanation:
Runs all pending database migrations.

---

22. Check migration status

php artisan migrate:status

Explanation:
Shows which migrations have already been executed.

---

23. Roll back the last migration batch

php artisan migrate:rollback

Explanation:
Reverses the most recent batch of migrations.

---

24. Roll back one migration

php artisan migrate:rollback --step=1

Explanation:
Rolls back one migration step.

---

25. Roll back multiple migrations

php artisan migrate:rollback --step=3

Explanation:
Rolls back the last 3 migration steps.

---

26. Reset all migrations

php artisan migrate:reset

Explanation:
Rolls back all migrations.

The database tables are removed according to the migration
rollback definitions.

---

27. Refresh migrations

php artisan migrate:refresh

Explanation:
Rolls back all migrations and runs them again.

Useful during development.

---

28. Refresh migrations with seeders

php artisan migrate:refresh --seed

Explanation:
Refreshes the database and then runs the seeders.

---

29. Delete all tables and migrate again

php artisan migrate:fresh

Explanation:
Drops all tables and runs all migrations again.

WARNING:
This deletes existing database data.

Use mainly for local development.

---

30. Fresh database + seed

php artisan migrate:fresh --seed

Explanation:
Drops all tables, runs migrations, and runs database seeders.

Very useful when rebuilding a development database.

WARNING:
Do NOT use this on a production database.

---

==================================================
6. SEEDERS
==========

31. Create a seeder

php artisan make:seeder ProductSeeder

Explanation:
Creates:

database/seeders/ProductSeeder.php

---

32. Run all seeders

php artisan db:seed

Explanation:
Runs the DatabaseSeeder.

---

33. Run a specific seeder

php artisan db:seed --class=ProductSeeder

Explanation:
Runs only ProductSeeder.

---

34. Migration + seed

php artisan migrate --seed

Explanation:
Runs pending migrations and then runs seeders.

---

35. Fresh database + seed

php artisan migrate:fresh --seed

Explanation:
Drops all tables, recreates them, and inserts seed data.

Very useful during local development.

---

