30. DO NOT LEAVE dd() EVERYWHERE
================================

During development:

dd($request->all());

is useful.

But before committing code, remove temporary dd()
statements.

---

## INSTEAD OF PERMANENT dd():

Use:

Log::info(...)

Log::warning(...)

Log::error(...)

or use:

Xdebug

Laravel Telescope

---

## IMPORTANT:

Do not leave sensitive request data, passwords, tokens,
authentication headers, or personal information in logs.

